{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159816",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 133,
      "videoOrder": 123,
      "sourceHash": "4f1c32e994b0847a4a1aef6500d2da7d0f447e7542ab3bd64b33ad244fa761f2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 4.08,
          "en": "And that's now it for this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.08,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "In this section, we had a in-depth look into NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.28,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "using this App Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 13.29,
          "en": "and you learned how you can set up routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.29,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "by using the file system instead of app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "and by using these special file names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 22.152,
          "en": "like page.js and layout.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.152,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "You also learned about other special files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 28.14,
          "en": "like error.js for handling errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.14,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "or not-found.js for handling not found errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 34.53,
          "en": "or the loading js file, which I'm not using here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 36.6,
          "en": "but which we used temporarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.6,
          "end": 39.42,
          "en": "to show some loading state on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.42,
          "end": 42.66,
          "en": "Though you learned that you have more granular control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.66,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "by using suspense, which is what we then did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "Now you also learned how to configure dynamic routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "where some path segments aren't known in advance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 58.8,
          "en": "like here, where we load pages for individual meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "where we don't know in advance how many meals we'll have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 66.659,
          "en": "and most importantly, you learned that all those pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.659,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "in the end just export standard React components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 72.93,
          "en": "but that those components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "are kind of special when using NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 78.69,
          "en": "That they are server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 81.39,
          "en": "that are executed on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.39,
          "end": 83.763,
          "en": "that are rendered on the server, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.63,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "And it's not just those page components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "but instead all components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 93.24000000000001,
          "en": "unless you explicitly opt out of this behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.24000000000001,
          "end": 97.59,
          "en": "by adding this use client directive to convert a file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.59,
          "end": 100.86,
          "en": "and its components into a client component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.86,
          "end": 103.89,
          "en": "which then is rendered on the client and which then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.89,
          "end": 108.18,
          "en": "therefore may use client side functionality like useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "or handling user events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.64,
          "end": 114,
          "en": "You therefore also learned that you can take advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114,
          "end": 117.78,
          "en": "of those Server components by fetching data directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.78,
          "end": 119.82,
          "en": "inside of those components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.82,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "There is no need to use user effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "and send requests to separate backends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 128.1,
          "en": "Instead, you can fetch the data from right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.1,
          "end": 130.68,
          "en": "inside your Server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "And you can just fetch the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 138.29,
          "en": "you also learned about Server Actions, async functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 142.32,
          "en": "that either have to use Server directive inside of them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.32,
          "end": 146.97,
          "en": "or that are stored in a file with used Server at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.97,
          "end": 150.69,
          "en": "And the special thing about those Server Actions is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.69,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "that you can assign them as values to the action prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 159.39,
          "en": "on form elements, either directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.39,
          "end": 162.393,
          "en": "or as we're doing it here with help of useFormState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.98,
          "end": 167.01,
          "en": "which is a hook provided by react-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.01,
          "end": 172.01,
          "en": "to handle responses returned by the Server action function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.07999999999998,
          "end": 176.88,
          "en": "and then potentially update the UI based on those responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.88,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "Like here where we are conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 181.92,
          "en": "showing an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.92,
          "end": 185.73,
          "en": "Speaking of updating the UI based on Server Actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "you also learned about the useFormStatus hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 192.24,
          "en": "which can be used to find out whether a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.24,
          "end": 193.83,
          "en": "is currently being submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.83,
          "end": 198.51,
          "en": "or not, which can then be used to update the UI accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "Now, related to all of that, you also learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "that NextJS does some pretty aggressive caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 210.66,
          "en": "and that therefore you should call revalidatePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 214.05,
          "en": "whenever you change some data to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.05,
          "end": 216.09,
          "en": "that the latest data is fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.09,
          "end": 219.12,
          "en": "and represented on your pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.12,
          "end": 221.73,
          "en": "And you also saw that it can be dangerous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 224.81,
          "en": "if you never test your app in production mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.81,
          "end": 227.67000000000002,
          "en": "because everything worked in development mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 228.75,
          "en": "in our app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.75,
          "end": 232.53,
          "en": "but then suddenly the data was missing in production mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.53,
          "end": 235.68,
          "en": "So this is an important function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.68,
          "end": 238.983,
          "en": "and an important concept to understand in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.66,
          "end": 244.89,
          "en": "Now, last but not least, we also talked about metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "that can be added to pages, static metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 252.9,
          "en": "as we have it here or dynamically generated metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.9,
          "end": 254.91,
          "en": "And therefore at this point you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.91,
          "end": 258.3,
          "en": "have a super solid NextJS foundation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.3,
          "end": 260.55,
          "en": "and you are ready to use NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.55,
          "end": 263.853,
          "en": "with its App Router in your future projects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
